@startuml
title Rewards Delivery - BIAN Control Record UML
' Machine-readable reconstruction of the raster BIAN Control Record diagram
' Service Domain: Rewards Delivery
' Source image: rewards-delivery-bom-uml.png
' BIAN source: https://bian.org/servicelandscape-14-0-0/views/view_52403.html
' Extraction: raster reconstruction; labels normalized where legible
hide methods
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
left to right direction

class "Rewards Delivery" as SD <<ServiceDomain>>
class "Rewards Delivery Procedure" as CRT <<ControlRecord>>
class "Procedure" as GA <<GenericArtifact>>
class "Workstep" as BQT <<BehaviorQualifierType>>

class "CR Rewards Delivery Procedure Instance Record" as CRI <<ControlRecordInstance>> {
  + Rewards Delivery Procedure Status : Status
  + Rewards Delivery Procedure Type : ProcessType
  + Rewards Delivery Procedure Requested Option : Text
  + Rewards Delivery Procedure Agent : Identifier
  + Rewards Delivery Procedure Result : Result
  + Rewards Delivery Procedure Event or Activity Instance : Identifier
  + Rewards Delivery Procedure Payment Structure : Identifier
  + Rewards Delivery Procedure Confirmation or Verification : Identifier
  + Rewards Delivery Procedure Reference : Identifier
  + Rewards Delivery Procedure Product and Service Type : ProductServiceType
  + Rewards Delivery Procedure Applied Service Instance : Identifier
  + Rewards Delivery Procedure Customer Type : CustomerType
  + Rewards Delivery Procedure Status Type : StatusType
  + Rewards Delivery Procedure Product and Service : Product
  + Rewards Delivery Procedure Financial or Transaction Arrangement : Agreement
  + Rewards Delivery Procedure Transaction : Transaction
  + Rewards Delivery Procedure Customer or Provider Advice : Identifier
  + Rewards Delivery Procedure Delivery Procedure : Procedure
}

SD "1" --> "1" CRT : defines control record
CRT "1" --> "0..*" CRI : instantiated as
CRT --> GA : conforms to generic artifact
GA --> BQT : qualified by

note right of CRI
  Source was a low-resolution PNG-only BIAN diagram.
  Text has been normalized for machine-readable context.
end note

@enduml
